# Death by starvation erases the save, and Continue goes with it.
#
# Starvation is the one death a script cannot stage out of the existing flags: it needs all four humor
# queues critical (entirely black bile), which in play is the end of a long run of bad organs and long
# journeys. --black-bile forces that state directly. It is not a special-cased death — a critical
# queue is a state every consumption path already handles, and travel simply cannot pay its vital-heat
# debt from queues that have nothing left to give.
#
# This death used to wait for the journey: heat was paid leg by leg, and the run ended between two
# cells. It no longer waits. Spent humors are now reckoned by the standing check that reckons wounds,
# so a body with all four queues critical is dead as soon as anything looks at it — and --black-bile
# sours them at the moment the protagonist is accepted, before the world has been touched. The run
# therefore ends on reaching the map, with no journey attempted.
#
# The leg-by-leg drain is still there and still fires first while a route is being walked, since it
# notices the queues empty in the same breath as it empties them. What this script now covers is the
# state being lethal on sight; death_narration_humors.cli covers a body that starves DURING a visit,
# which is where the save-still-exists assertion moved to.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --black-bile --allow-reentry --save-path .tmp-cli-save/death-starve.json

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue

# No travel, and no click: the check is standing, so reaching the map is enough.
wait mode Death 45
expect STARVATION
expect END RUN

expect-state savefile save none

click end-run
wait mode MainMenu 20
# Continue is state, not pixels — a disabled button differs only by colour on screen, so
# this is asserted through inspect rather than by scanning the terminal.
inspect menu
expect-state menu Continue disabled

quit
